144. Preorder Traversal

Explanation:
Preorder is root left right

But here we need help of recursive function as we need to go down the depth
Create a global ans array
have a helper function in here and put root in it
For the helper function to run
if node is null - return -> it is a void function simple return is enough
in ans first add node.value
then preorder node.left and preorder node..right - recursive function

Code:
/**
 * Definition for a binary tree node.
 * public class TreeNode {
 *     int val;
 *     TreeNode left;
 *     TreeNode right;
 *     TreeNode() {}
 *     TreeNode(int val) { this.val = val; }
 *     TreeNode(int val, TreeNode left, TreeNode right) {
 *         this.val = val;
 *         this.left = left;
 *         this.right = right;
 *     }
 * }
 */
class Solution {
    List<Integer> ans = new ArrayList<>();
    public List<Integer> preorderTraversal(TreeNode root) {
        preOrder(root);
        return ans;
    }

    public void preOrder(TreeNode node){
        if(node==null){
            return;
        }

        ans.add(node.val);
        preOrder(node.left);
        preOrder(node.right);
    }
}
